# Separate revision ZIPs and current reading copies

The current manuscript or research head for each collection remains unpacked at the path in the [paper catalog](<paper_catalog.json>) and [workspace index](<../README.md>). Original delivery ZIPs were retained unchanged. Twelve older revision folders or note versions that lacked a distinct convenient ZIP now have one under their paper's `Revision_Archives` directory. The [creation receipt](<REVISION_ARCHIVES_2026-09-30.json>) lists every member's source path, size and SHA-256 plus each new ZIP hash. All 54 members passed ZIP CRC and independent content comparison with their loose sources.

These ZIPs are **separate revision snapshots**, not new paper identities. Existing loose older folders remain in place to preserve original paths, reproducibility scripts and historical links; no source file was deleted or moved. Thus the newest work is easy to read unpacked, but older loose layouts have not yet been retired. A ZIP-only historical layout would require a later dependency/link audit and separate authorization to remove or relocate the loose originals.

The workspace `.gitignore` excludes `*.zip`, including these new archives and the original delivery ZIPs. They are local filesystem artifacts with hash receipts, not Git-tracked backups.

